<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DI/" xmlns:lex="https://lexipedia.xyz/ns/lex/1.0" id="dmn_ca_bpc_480" name="Cal. BPC § 480: denial of a license for a conviction or prior discipline" namespace="https://lexipedia.xyz/ns/decision/ca_bpc_480" exporter="lexflow (design prototype)" exporterVersion="0.1">
  <description>Decision requirements for Cal. Bus. &amp; Prof. Code § 480(a)-(d) and (h), text of open-us-law v2026.09.1. Precedence is carried by the DRD, not by rule order: grounds (a)(1)/(a)(2) &lt;- 'However' exceptions (a)(1)(A)/(B) &lt;- 'Notwithstanding' bars (b)/(c), every table UNIQUE.  Draft for review, not legal advice.</description>
  <extensionElements>
    <lex:model id="ca.bpc_480" jurisdiction="ca" jurisdictionName="California" reviewStatus="draft" method="assistant-edited" consumer="lexflow:process:ca.license_conviction" section="lexflow:statute:ca:Cal. BPC § 480" actId="STATE_CA_Cbpc_D1.5_C2_S480"/>
  </extensionElements>
  <inputData id="in_application_date" name="application_date" label="Date of application">
    <description>The date the application was made: every seven-year window in (a) runs back from it.</description>
    <variable id="in_application_date_var" name="application_date" typeRef="date"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_offense" name="offense" label="Offense of conviction (code and section, with the record of conviction)">
    <description>Read by the classification findings serious_felony and fiduciary_financial_felony, with the record of conviction: some § 1192.7(c) items turn on how the offense was committed. The registration tier is the separate input sex_offender_tier, because PEN § 290(d) does not assign the tier from the offense alone.</description>
    <variable id="in_offense_var" name="offense" typeRef="string"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_sex_offender_tier" name="sex_offender_tier" label="Sex offender registration tier under PEN § 290(d), as ascertained">
    <description>The tier the person registers in under Penal Code § 290(d). It is an input, not a finding on the offense, because § 290(d) does not assign the tier from the offense alone. The factors: (d)(1) tier one: a registrable misdemeanor, or a registrable felony that is not a serious or violent felony under § 667.5(c) or § 1192.7(c); (d)(2) tier two: a registrable offense also described in § 667.5(c) or § 1192.7(c), § 285, § 286(g) or (h), § 287(g) or (h), § 289(b), or a second or subsequent § 647.6 conviction brought and tried separately; (d)(3) tier three: a later conviction, in a separate proceeding, of a violent felony after a registrable conviction ((A)); commitment as a sexually violent predator under Welf. &amp; Inst. Code §§ 6600 et seq. ((B)); conviction of an offense listed in (C) or (I)-(R); a SARATSO risk level of well above average at release ((D)); habitual sex offender status under § 667.71 ((E)); two separately tried § 288(a) convictions ((F)); a sentence of 15 to 25 years to life under § 667.61 ((G)); registration under § 290.004 ((H)); (d)(4): registration under § 290.005 (another jurisdiction's offense or registration duty); (d)(5): the Department of Justice may place a person in a tier-to-be-determined category and must ascertain the tier within 24 months. The model takes the tier as ascertained: a tier-to-be-determined placement must be resolved first. Allowed values: "none", "tier_one", "tier_two", "tier_three".</description>
    <variable id="in_sex_offender_tier_var" name="sex_offender_tier" typeRef="string"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_disposition" name="disposition" label="Disposition of the arrest">
    <description>"conviction" in the sense of BPC § 7.5(a), first sentence: a judgment following a plea or verdict of guilty, a plea of nolo contendere, or a finding of guilt (480(h)); "other" for an arrest that ended in anything else, including an infraction, citation or juvenile adjudication (480(d)). Whether a conviction is final for board action is the separate input conviction_final. Allowed values: "conviction", "other".</description>
    <extensionElements>
      <lex:term term="conviction" key="lexflow:term:ca:Cal. BPC § 7.5:conviction" wikidata="Q2916183" match="exact" matchSource="fixtures/xref/wikidata_terms.json"/>
    </extensionElements>
    <variable id="in_disposition_var" name="disposition" typeRef="string"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_conviction_date" name="conviction_date" label="Date of conviction">
    <description>Date of the judgment (BPC § 7.5(a)).</description>
    <variable id="in_conviction_date_var" name="conviction_date" typeRef="date"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_conviction_final" name="conviction_final" label="Conviction final for board action (BPC § 7.5(a))">
    <description>true when the time for appeal has elapsed, the judgment of conviction has been affirmed on appeal, or an order granting probation has been made suspending the imposition of sentence. BPC § 7.5(a), second sentence, lets a board take an action that follows a conviction only then; 480(h) brings § 7.5 in. Read only when disposition is "conviction" (conviction_ground r7).</description>
    <variable id="in_conviction_final_var" name="conviction_final" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_presently_incarcerated" name="presently_incarcerated" label="Presently incarcerated for that crime">
    <description>(a)(1), second limb. Taken as given: the text does not say whether "presently" means on the date of application or when the board decides (see incarceration_recent).</description>
    <variable id="in_presently_incarcerated_var" name="presently_incarcerated" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_release_date" name="release_date" label="Date released from incarceration for that crime">
    <description>null when never incarcerated or still incarcerated.</description>
    <variable id="in_release_date_var" name="release_date" typeRef="date"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_profession" name="profession" label="License applied for (licensing unit of the BPC)">
    <description>The units listed in (a)(1)(B)(i)-(v); every other license is "other" (including other Chapter 12 licenses, which (iv) does not list). Allowed values: "bpc_d3_ch6_professional_fiduciary", "bpc_d3_ch9_contractor", "bpc_d3_ch11_3_private_investigator", "bpc_d3_ch12_funeral_director", "bpc_d3_ch12_cemetery_manager", "bpc_d4_real_estate", "other".</description>
    <variable id="in_profession_var" name="profession" typeRef="string"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_substantially_related" name="substantially_related" label="Crime substantially related to the qualifications, functions, or duties of the profession">
    <description>A finding of the board, made with the criteria each board must adopt under BPC § 481 (§ 480 does not cite § 481; § 481(a) points back at denials).</description>
    <extensionElements>
      <lex:requires status="lexflow:status:ca:crime-substantially-related" providedBy="lexflow:process:ca.license_conviction" element="decide_ground" evidence="finding" via="Cal. BPC § 481"/>
    </extensionElements>
    <variable id="in_substantially_related_var" name="substantially_related" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_certificate_of_rehabilitation" name="certificate_of_rehabilitation" label="Holds a certificate of rehabilitation (Penal Code §§ 4852.01 et seq.)">
    <description>Produced by a superior-court proceeding under Penal Code Chapter 3.5 of Title 6 of Part 3; no lexflow model yet.</description>
    <extensionElements>
      <lex:requires status="lexflow:status:ca:certificate-of-rehabilitation" providedBy="lexflow:process:ca.certificate_of_rehabilitation" evidence="document" via="Cal. PEN § 4852.01"/>
      <lex:term term="certificate of rehabilitation" match="none" matchSource="fixtures/xref/wikidata_terms.json"/>
    </extensionElements>
    <variable id="in_certificate_of_rehabilitation_var" name="certificate_of_rehabilitation" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_pardon_or_clemency" name="pardon_or_clemency" label="Granted clemency or a pardon by a state or federal executive">
    <description>No section is cited; the executive acts outside this code.</description>
    <extensionElements>
      <lex:requires status="lexflow:status:ca:pardon-or-clemency" evidence="document"/>
      <lex:term term="pardon" key="lexflow:concept:pardon" wikidata="Q537151" match="exact" matchSource="fixtures/xref/wikidata_terms.json"/>
    </extensionElements>
    <variable id="in_pardon_or_clemency_var" name="pardon_or_clemency" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_showing_of_rehabilitation" name="showing_of_rehabilitation" label="Has made a showing of rehabilitation under BPC § 482">
    <description>Decided by the board itself under § 482(b), from the evidence the applicant submits (step submit_rehab_evidence of the same process).</description>
    <extensionElements>
      <lex:requires status="lexflow:status:ca:showing-of-rehabilitation-482" providedBy="lexflow:process:ca.license_conviction" element="submit_rehab_evidence" evidence="finding" via="Cal. BPC § 482"/>
      <lex:term term="rehabilitation" key="lexflow:concept:rehabilitation" wikidata="Q2142602" match="exact" matchSource="fixtures/xref/wikidata_terms.json"/>
    </extensionElements>
    <variable id="in_showing_of_rehabilitation_var" name="showing_of_rehabilitation" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_conviction_dismissed" name="conviction_dismissed" label="Conviction dismissed under Penal Code § 1203.4, 1203.4a, 1203.41, 1203.42 or 1203.425 (or a comparable dismissal or expungement)">
    <description>Produced by the dismissal process (lexflow model ca.record_sealing, decision dismissal_relief, outcome dismissed) or by automatic relief under § 1203.425; proof is required when the DOJ report does not show it (480(c)).</description>
    <extensionElements>
      <lex:requires status="lexflow:status:ca:conviction-dismissed" providedBy="lexflow:process:ca.record_sealing" element="dismissed" evidence="register" via="Cal. PEN § 1203.4; Cal. PEN § 1203.4a; Cal. PEN § 1203.41; Cal. PEN § 1203.42; Cal. PEN § 1203.425"/>
      <lex:term term="expungement" key="lexflow:concept:expungement" wikidata="Q2352928" match="exact" matchSource="fixtures/xref/wikidata_terms.json"/>
    </extensionElements>
    <variable id="in_conviction_dismissed_var" name="conviction_dismissed" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_formal_discipline" name="formal_discipline" label="Subjected to formal discipline by a licensing board in or outside California">
    <description>(a)(2).</description>
    <variable id="in_formal_discipline_var" name="formal_discipline" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_discipline_date" name="discipline_date" label="Date of the formal discipline">
    <description>null when there was none or the date is not known. A null date, or one after the date of application, is neither within the preceding seven years (discipline_recent) nor earlier than seven years preceding the date of application (discipline_older), so neither sentence of (a)(2) makes it a ground (discipline_ground r9).</description>
    <variable id="in_discipline_date_var" name="discipline_date" typeRef="date"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_misconduct_cause" name="misconduct_cause_for_discipline" label="Based on professional misconduct that would have been cause for discipline before this board">
    <description>(a)(2).</description>
    <variable id="in_misconduct_cause_var" name="misconduct_cause_for_discipline" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_discipline_related" name="discipline_substantially_related" label="Discipline substantially related to the qualifications, functions, or duties of the profession">
    <description>(a)(2).</description>
    <variable id="in_discipline_related_var" name="discipline_substantially_related" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_discipline_rests_on_conviction" name="discipline_rests_on_conviction" label="The discipline was based on the conviction (the acts underlying it)">
    <description>Links the discipline to the conviction this evaluation is about (one conviction and one discipline record per evaluation).</description>
    <variable id="in_discipline_rests_on_conviction_var" name="discipline_rests_on_conviction" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_sexual_misconduct" name="sexual_misconduct_726_729" label="Discipline was for conduct that would be sexual abuse, misconduct or relations with a patient (BPC § 726) or sexual exploitation (BPC § 729(a)) by a physician and surgeon">
    <description>Only matters for discipline older than seven years ((a)(2), last sentence).</description>
    <variable id="in_sexual_misconduct_var" name="sexual_misconduct_726_729" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
