  <decision id="d_serious_felony" name="serious_felony" label="(a)(1)(A) Serious felony as defined in PEN § 1192.7(c)?">
    <description>(a)(1)(A) Serious felony as defined in PEN § 1192.7(c)? [finding: no executable logic] A closed list in Penal Code § 1192.7(c). Most items name an offense, but some turn on how it was committed ((c)(8): personally inflicting great bodily injury, or personally using a firearm; (c)(23): personally using a dangerous or deadly weapon), so the finding reads the record of conviction, not only the code section. A lookup the model does not encode (a BKM candidate).</description>
    <extensionElements>
      <lex:finding basis="A closed list in Penal Code § 1192.7(c). Most items name an offense, but some turn on how it was committed ((c)(8): personally inflicting great bodily injury, or personally using a firearm; (c)(23): personally using a dangerous or deadly weapon), so the finding reads the record of conviction, not only the code section. A lookup the model does not encode (a BKM candidate)."/>
      <lex:governedBy key="lexflow:statute:ca:Cal. BPC § 480" pinpoint="(a)(1)(A)"/>
    </extensionElements>
    <variable id="d_serious_felony_var" name="serious_felony" typeRef="boolean"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_d_serious_felony__in_offense">
      <requiredInput href="#in_offense"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <authorityRequirement id="ar_d_serious_felony__ks_480_a1A">
      <requiredAuthority href="#ks_480_a1A"/>
    </authorityRequirement>
    <authorityRequirement id="ar_d_serious_felony__ks_pen_1192_7">
      <requiredAuthority href="#ks_pen_1192_7"/>
    </authorityRequirement>
  </decision>
  <decision id="d_fiduciary_felony" name="fiduciary_financial_felony" label="(a)(1)(B) Financial felony directly and adversely related to fiduciary duties (board regulations)?">
    <description>(a)(1)(B) Financial felony directly and adversely related to fiduciary duties (board regulations)? [finding: no executable logic] Classified by the board's own regulations, which are outside the statute index.</description>
